title:: BMPluginSpec
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - a single channel strip in a BMTrimPluginsRack
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMTrimPluginsStrip manages trim and plugin settings for an individual channel of a link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsRack::. Trim settings are applied to the input signal first, and then each plugin in the specified order.

warning:: Under normal circumstances you would not create instances of these directly, rather they would be created for you by a BMTrimPluginsRack, and you would access them using its strong::at:: method. (See examples below). Thus only user-relevant methods are documented here.
::

See also: link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsRack::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMPlugin::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsStripGUI::

INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: trim
Set or get this channel's trim value in dBFS. The inital setting for this is 0, i.e. full scale.
				
method:: plugins
Returns a link::Classes/List:: containing this strip's link::Classes/Plugins/BMPlugin:: instances in the order in which they are applied to the signal.
				

method:: clear
Remove all plugins from this strip.


method:: addPlugin
Add a plugin to this strip, at the end of its chain of plugins.

argument:: plugin
A link::Classes/Plugins/BMPlugin::.


method:: removePlugin
Remove a plugin from this strip's chain of plugins.

argument:: indexOrPlugin
Either the index of the plugin to remove or the link::Classes/Plugins/BMPlugin:: itself.


method:: movePluginUp
Move a plugin up one position in this strip's chain of plugins.

argument:: index
The index of the plugin to move.


method:: movePluginDown
Move a plugin down one position in this strip's chain of plugins.

argument:: index
The index of the plugin to move.


Examples::

code::
// 5.1 Array
(
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

r = BMTrimPluginsRack(l, name: 'Plug em In');

r[\L]; // get the BMTrimPluginsStrip for 'L'

// plugins are added at the end of the chain
r[\L].addPlugin(BMPlugin('3 Band EQ'));
r[\L].addPlugin(BMPlugin(\Highpass));
r[\L].addPlugin(BMPlugin(\Lowpass));
r[\L].plugins; // check order

// but you can move them
r[\L].movePluginUp(2);
r[\L].movePluginDown(0);
r[\L].plugins; // check order

// remove by index
r[\L].removePlugin(0);
r[\L].plugins;

r.gui; // play with the GUI

r.free;
::
